An instruction for a later todo, given mid-plan: the user plans three todos
and has the first done; then, before the second, says how the third must be
done. The third is done in a new session, which knows only what mem kept, so
the instruction must be kept in mem (a thought, a fact or the todo's own
words), not left in a conversation that a pop or a new session drops.

-- project/go.mod --
module serve

go 1.22
-- project/main.go --
// Command serve answers "ok" on every path.
package main

import (
	"fmt"
	"log"
	"net/http"
)

const addr = ":8080"

func main() {
	http.HandleFunc("/", func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
		fmt.Fprintln(w, "ok")
	})
	log.Fatal(http.ListenAndServe(addr, nil))
}
-- project/README.md --
# serve

serve answers "ok" on every path.

    go run .

It listens on port 8080.
-- prompt --
Plan this as todos in mem: (1) make the port a --port flag in main.go, keeping 8080 as the default; (2) document the flag in README.md; (3) add a test for the flag's default. Do only the first todo now.
-- prompt --
Before you go on: when you get to the test, it must be table-driven, be called TestPortDefaults, and also check that --port 0 is refused with an error. Now do the second todo only.
-- prompt-new --
Carry on with the plan in mem: do what's left.
-- check --
after 1 file main.go contains flag
after 2 file README.md contains -port
turn 1 tool gnovm_run >= 1
turn 3 tool gnovm_run >= 1
cmd grep -rq 'func TestPortDefaults' --include='*_test.go' .
cmd go test ./...
cmd timeout 60 go run . --port 0; s=$?; [ $s -ne 0 ] && [ $s -ne 124 ]
vm-dump contains TestPortDefaults
mem-count open == 0
